  "description": "Replacement of existing timber-framed windows with uPVC alternatives at third and fourth storeys and replacement of existing timber front door and balcony door with composite front door and upvc glazed balcony door\n\nThe application seeks permission to replace deteriorating single-glazed timber windows with modern uPVC units at the third and fourth floors of a four-storey residential building. The proposed windows will match the existing ones in style, dimensions, and glazing configuration. The changes are intended to improve thermal performance, reduce maintenance demands, and enhance occupant comfort. The proposed doors will match existing doors in style and dimensions, but the rear door (the balcony door) will slightly differ in glazing configuration to allow more light into the property. The rear (balcony) door is not visible at street level.\n\nThe flat is not located in a conservation area, is not listed, and the affected windows are not visible from street level or the public realm. Due to the height of the property, regular maintenance of timber windows is impractical and costly. High-quality uPVC windows offer a long-term, visually consistent, and energy-efficient solution that has already been adopted in other parts of the estate.\n\nSupporting photographs and product specifications are provided. A full Design and Access Statement is also submitted with this application.\n",
